cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use wsr, please cite it as below. If you use its repair agent, please also cite the weight-space
  programming work it builds on (listed under references).
title: "wsr: Weight-Space Repair"
abstract: >-
  Find out why an open-weight language model gave a bad reply (a chat template, a sampler setting, a truncated
  context, a quantised tensor, or the weights), and fix it at the right level: a setting, an activation steering
  or a verified weight edit, accepted only by a statistical judge on held-out data.
type: software
authors:
